Subject: [PATCH 4/4] test(parakeet): integration + C++ unit tests for VAD
 streaming
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds two test layers covering the new VAD-driven simulated-streaming path:

- C++ unit tests (addon/tests/StreamingProcessorTest.cpp) wired into the
  existing parakeet_tests GoogleTest target. Cover the public defaults of
  StreamingProcessor::Config (sample-rate, VAD thresholds, derived
  sample-domain values, partial-decode cadence) and the Transcript struct
  defaults (isPartial=false on both constructors). Header-only — no model
  files required, runs in any CI lane that already builds parakeet_tests.

- JS integration tests (test/integration/vad-streaming-simulation.test.js)
  exercising TranscriptionParakeet.runStreaming end-to-end:
    * final segment delivery and clean session shutdown,
    * mid-segment partial emission when partial_decode_interval_ms is set,
    * cancel re-entrancy (a second runStreaming after a cancelled job
      must not fail with "Streaming session already active").
  The suite skips cleanly when silero_vad.onnx or sample.raw are missing
  from the local checkout, mirroring the conditional-skip pattern used by
  external-data-staging.test.js.
